anv (macOS): resolve the optional entrypoints to NULL at link time instead of by dynamic lookup

vk_entrypoints_gen.py --weak declares every entrypoint a driver may implement as weak, so the entrypoint tables hold
NULL for the ones it does not: ELF resolves weak undefined symbols to 0, MSVC points them at vk_entrypoint_stub with
/alternatename (and vk_dispatch_table_gen.py skips the stub). ld64 has no weak undefined symbols outside of dylib
imports and accepts them only with -undefined dynamic_lookup (as kosmickrisp and lavapipe link on darwin). Each of
them then becomes a flat-namespace lookup that dyld resolves by searching every loaded image when the driver is
loaded: 10986 for anv (anv/gfx*/vk_common/wsi/... tables), ~390 ms per dlopen of libvulkan_intel.dylib, paid by every
process that creates a Metal device or a VideoToolbox session on the B580.

Link the driver twice on darwin: once as before (libvulkan_intel_unresolved, not installed), then
vk_entrypoints_null_macho.py lists the symbols that link left to dynamic lookup and writes an assembly file defining
each weak one as an absolute 0 with private extern visibility, and the real driver is linked with that file and
without -undefined dynamic_lookup. Every table entry for an entrypoint the driver lacks is NULL at link time, as on
ELF; nothing is looked up at load time any more. A non-weak symbol left to dynamic lookup is a real missing
dependency and fails the build: there was one, NSNumber from wsi_common_metal_layer.m, so the macOS WSI dependency
now lists Foundation (it was only found because some other image had loaded Foundation).

B580 hackintosh (x86_64 macOS): dlopen of libvulkan_intel.dylib 390 ms -> 3.4 ms (cold after purge
673 -> 217 ms; with AppKit/Metal/VideoToolbox/AVFoundation already loaded 406 -> 1.1 ms); MTLCreateSystemDefaultDevice
411 -> 22 ms; a vtdecq process 0.72 -> 0.33 s. vkGetInstanceProcAddr/vkGetDeviceProcAddr resolve the same 865
commands identically (all 15 instance and 210 device extensions enabled); Metal compute/render, VideoToolbox decode
(per-frame md5) and H.264/HEVC/AV1 encode (byte-identical streams) unchanged.

